==============================================================================================
WHAT THIS ROUND IS
==============================================================================================
  Two kernel binaries from the same tree, same commit, same compiler and flags,
  differing in one constant's value: kFlowPathRecomputeInterval, seconds(1) vs
  microseconds(1000). Built 2026-08-31 by the E round and never run until now.
  Arms are interleaved in time and the order is counterbalanced (PREREG.md 4).
  => a difference between the arms IS attributable to that constant.
  Build type is Debug (-O0), as in every prior round. Not release numbers.

==============================================================================================
GUARD -- did the two arms of each pair do the same work?
==============================================================================================
  iperf3's own packet count and aggregate tx from /proc/net/dev. Out of band => the
  pair is dropped, because its difference would be a traffic difference.

          pair   1hz packets  1khz packets   1hz Mbit/s  1khz Mbit/s   ratio  verdict
       zero r1     5,357,127     5,357,127        617.5        617.3   1.000  ok
       zero r2     5,357,127     5,357,127        617.4        617.4   1.000  ok
       zero r3     5,357,127     5,357,127        617.5        617.6   1.000  ok
      s1024 r1     5,357,127     5,357,127        617.3        617.3   1.000  ok
      s1024 r2     5,357,127     5,357,127        617.3        617.6   1.000  ok
      s1024 r3     5,357,127     5,357,127        617.3        617.7   1.001  ok

